        "content": "Based on the GitHub page provided, here's the extracted information:\n\n**Creation Date:** July 28, 2026\n\n**Description:** \"Makes your AI agent think like the laziest senior dev in the room. The best code is the code you never wrote.\"\n\n**What It Does:** Ponytail is an agent skill that prevents AI assistants from over-engineering code. Before writing any code, the agent follows a \"ladder\" of simplification:\n\n1. Checks if the feature is needed at all (YAGNI principle)\n2. Looks for existing code in the repository to reuse\n3. Checks if the standard library can handle it\n4. Verifies if the platform already provides it\n5. Looks for existing dependencies\n6. Determines if it can be solved with one line\n7. Only then writes the minimal solution\n\nThe tool promises \"54% less code, 20% cheaper, 27% faster\" while maintaining 100% of safety guards like validation, error handling, and security.\n\n**Release Information:** \n- Latest release shows 1 tag and 1 package\n- Licensed under MIT\n- Works with multiple AI coding agents including Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI, OpenCode, Pi, Antigravity, Hermes, and OpenClaw\n- Available as npm package: `@0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved`\n\nThe project demonstrates measurable improvements, with documentation noting that on tasks where \"agents over-build hardest, the drop reaches 94% less code.\""
      }
    ]
  },
