        "content": "Based on the GitHub repository content:\n\n**Creation Date:** August 2, 2026 (15:58:29 UTC)\n\n**Description:** \"Autonomous, headless Android debugger designed for AI coding agents\"\n\n**What It Does:** Debroid is a headless command-line interface that communicates using the Java Debug Wire Protocol (JDWP). It enables AI coding agents like Claude Code, Grok Build, Codex, Cursor, and Antigravity to debug live Android applications without a GUI. The tool provides deterministic JSON output for machine parsing.\n\nKey capabilities include setting breakpoints, catching exceptions, monitoring field modifications with watchpoints, recursively inspecting object memory and variables, dynamically mutating variables, evaluating Java expressions, stepping through code execution, and extracting locals from Kotlin Continuation frames.\n\n**Launch/Release Information:**\n- Current branch: `main`\n- Latest commit OID: `f30fb720c72bfce42bc21c0f40ce12f58f6e4814`\n- Two releases published with associated tags\n- Installation available via pre-built binary or building from source\n- Apache 2.0 License"
