        "content": "# Axern - AI Agent Sandbox Platform\n\n**Creation Date:** July 28, 2026\n\n**Description:** \"Open-source sandboxes for AI agents, untrusted code execution, and durable services\"\n\n**What It Does:** Axern provides an open-source sandbox platform that isolates untrusted agent-generated code using runsc (gVisor) for secure execution, while running trusted long-lived services with runc through a unified resource and lifecycle model. The platform includes CLI and SDKs (Go, Python, TypeScript) with consistent APIs for environments, processes, files, services, storage, tunnels, and task evidence.\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Agent sandbox with runsc isolation boundary\n- Durable PostgreSQL-backed control plane\n- Support for both OCI and Nydus image formats\n- Agent execution with verification and evidence capture via Axrun\n- SSH-compatible terminals and reverse TCP tunnels\n\n**Release Status:** Pre-1.0, actively developed, suitable for evaluation and contribution but operators should review security boundaries before multi-tenant production deployment.\n\n**Installation:** Available via Homebrew (`brew install cofy-x/tap/axern`), standalone installer script, or Kubernetes Helm chart from OCI registry."
