        "content": "# agent-vision-toolkit - Repository Summary\n\n## Creation Date\nThe repository `Anionex/agent-vision-toolkit` was created on August 1, 2026.\n\n## Repository Description\nThe project is described as a \"vision toolkit and skill designed for text-only llms — image Q&A, long-screenshot OCR, frontend UI restoration, and GUI automation, with optional seamless integration for Codex, Claude Code, Pi, Oh My Pi, and OpenCode.\"\n\n## What This Tool Does\nThis toolkit enables text-only AI agents to handle visual tasks through two main components:\n\n1. **Vision tool CLIs** - Multiple command-line tools that any agent capable of invoking a shell can use\n\n2. **Seamless integration layer** - An optional local proxy and single-file native plugins allowing \"images we paste and the agent's built-in image tools both work seamlessly\" without extra tool installation\n\nThe toolkit includes specialized tools for different purposes:\n- `glance` - answering questions about images and OCR text transcription\n- `ground` - locating objects or regions and returning bounding box coordinates\n- `detect` - inventorying image elements with visible text and pixel positions\n- `trace` - recovering geometric trajectories from graphics as editable SVG primitives\n- `crop` - cutting pixel regions from images\n\n## Release Information\n- License: MIT License\n- Current version is on the `main` branch\n- One release tag is present in the repository\n- The project is verified and functional across multiple agent platforms (Codex, Claude Code, Pi, Oh My Pi, and OpenCode)"
